== Match report ==

=== Volisania 0–2 Balisca ===
Co-hosts [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] advanced to the semi-finals with a comfortable victory over [[Volisania national football team|Volisania]] in [[Martapura]]. Balisca scored twice in the first half, finding the net in the 30th and 42nd minutes, and their defense held firm for the remainder of the match to secure the clean sheet.

=== Asikyira 4–1 Pangkajene ===
[[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] delivered a dominant performance to thrash [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] in [[Axarquía]]. [[Amadou Baal]] opened the scoring in the 10th minute, [[Boubacar Sarr]] doubled the lead in the 15th, [[Idrissa Koné]] made it three before half-time (43'), and [[Ousmane Gueye]] added a fourth in the 70th minute. [[Andi Akbar]] scored a consolation for Pangkajene in the 86th minute, but Asikyira were comprehensive winners.

== Summary ==

The conclusion of the quarter-finals produced 7 goals across 2 matches. [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] and [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] advanced to the semi-finals. Asikyira's 4–1 victory was the most emphatic result of the day, with four different scorers finding the net.

The semi-final matchups are now confirmed:
* [[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] vs [[Orma national football team|Orma]] — 6 July, [[Castejón]]
* [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] vs [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] — 6 July, [[Concepción]]

